WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.130
A man walks into the
cinema without a ticket.

2
00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.700
In French: «Il est entré
sans payer.» English says:

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.870
he went in without paying.

4
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.560
So where is the -ing in the French?

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:11.920
It's not a one-off.

6
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.590
«J'aime chanter» is how
French says I like singing.

7
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.180
So when English reaches for -ing,

8
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.780
what does French reach for instead,

9
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.280
and why? In this mission,

10
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.840
you'll watch a gate that lets
only one kind of verb through.

11
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.560
Then you'll run verbs
through a factory that stamps

12
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.950
on a new ending, and test
every form in the lab.

13
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.280
Your mission: work out
which verb form French uses

14
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.110
after each little linking word.
